/-!
# A strong generator for the perfect derived category of a proper smooth scheme

Let `k` be a field and let `X` be a scheme proper and smooth over `k`. Then `D_perf(𝒪_X)` has a
*strong* generator: a single object `𝒢` and a single integer `n`, the same for every perfect
complex, with `⟨𝒢⟩ₙ = D_perf(𝒪_X)`. This is [Stacks, Tag 0FZ6].

## The shape of the source's argument

[Stacks, Tag 0FZ5] produces finite locally free `ℰ`, `𝒢` with `𝒪_Δ ∈ ⟨ℰ ⊠ 𝒢⟩` in
`D(𝒪_{X × X})`, and the source then takes `𝒢` for the strong generator. The argument is: write
`𝒪_Δ ∈ ⟨ℰ ⊠ 𝒢⟩ₙ` for one fixed `n` ([Stacks, Tag 0ATG], here
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.prop_triangEnvelope_iff`); for a perfect `K` push the whole
membership forward along the exact functor `Φ_K = R pr_{2,*}(L pr_1^* K ⊗^𝐋 −)`
([Stacks, Tag 0FX5]); use `Φ_K(𝒪_Δ) = K` ([Stacks, Tag 0FYV]) on the left and
`Φ_K(ℰ ⊠ 𝒢) = RΓ(X, K ⊗^𝐋 ℰ) ⊗_k 𝒢` ([Stacks, Tag 08EU]) on the right. Properness makes the
cohomology of `K ⊗^𝐋 ℰ` finite dimensional in each degree and perfectness makes it vanish
outside a bounded range, so the right-hand side is a finite direct sum of shifts of `𝒢`, that
is an object of `⟨𝒢⟩₀`. The level `n` does not move, because it is read off the *single* object
`𝒪_Δ` and not off `K`; this is exactly what makes the generator strong rather than merely
classical.

## What this file proves

The functorial step is proved here in the generality in which the source states it, as
`Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.triangEnvelopeIter_inverseImage_of_le`: an exact functor carrying
the objects of `P` into `⟨Q⟩₀` carries `⟨P⟩ₙ` into `⟨Q⟩ₙ` for every `n`. The geometric inputs
`𝒪_Δ ∈ ⟨ℰ ⊠ 𝒢⟩` and the two identities for `Φ_K` are carried as hypotheses of the main theorem;
see its `stacks` attribute for which, and with which tags.

`Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.isZero_of_isStrongTriangulatedGenerator_zero` records that the
conclusion is not satisfied by a degenerate witness: if the zero object strongly generates, every
object is zero.

## Main results

* `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.triangEnvelopeIter_inverseImage_of_le`: the stages of the
  triangulated envelope are functorial along an exact functor.
* `Stacks.TriangulatedGenerators.isZero_of_isStrongTriangulatedGenerator_zero`: only a zero
  category is strongly generated by its zero object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isStrongTriangulatedGenerator_of_diagonalEnvelope`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0FZ6]**, on the carried hypotheses listed in its attribute.

## Implementation notes

`D_perf(𝒪_X)` is `AlgebraicGeometry.perfectDerived X` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedVarieties/TransformedDiagonal/Basic.lean`, the full
subcategory of `Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect` objects of
`DerivedCategory X.Modules` at the locally small model
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.{u}` of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean`. That it is triangulated is
`Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectTriangulatedSubcategory.isTriangulated_isPerfect` on the ringed space
underlying `X`, which is stated at an arbitrary localization universe; the instance registered in
the library, `Stacks.Perfect.BoundedLocallyFreeComplexes.perfectDerivedProperty_isTriangulated`,
is pinned to `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` and so does not apply here. It is
re-read at the locally small model as
`AlgebraicGeometry.isTriangulated_isPerfect_locallySmall` and used as a local instance, so that
no new global instance competes with the pinned one.

`⟨E⟩` and `⟨E⟩ₙ` are `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope` and
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.triangEnvelopeIter` of
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.singleton E`; that these are the subcategories of Derived
Categories, Section 09SI is
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope_eq_iSup_and_isSaturated_and_le_iff`
([Stacks, Tag 0ATG]) in `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Triangulated/Generators.lean`. "Strong
generator" is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsStrongTriangulatedGenerator`, Mathlib's
`∃ n, ⟨E⟩ₙ = ⊤`, which carries `@[stacks 09SJ "(2)"]` in
`Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Triangulated/Generators.lean`. It is *not* the weak generator
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator` ([Stacks, Tag 09SJ](3)) of
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Triangulated/Generators.lean`.

